  Mobile  screenshot: (Image 3)

RECONSTRUCTION RULES
--------------------
R1. Reproduce ALL text content exactly as it appears in the screenshots —
    including headings, body text, navigation labels, sidebar text, footer
    columns, copyright notices, and link lists. Zoom in mentally on every
    region. Do not skip, summarise, or omit any visible text anywhere on the
    page. If a word is genuinely illegible, approximate it; never leave a
    visible text region empty.

R2. Use src="rick.jpg" for every <img> element, regardless of what images
    appear in the screenshots.

R3. Use href="#" for every <a> element.

R4. Match the visual design (colors, fonts, spacing, layout) as closely as
    possible using inline <style> or a <style> block in <head>.

R5. Infer responsive breakpoints from the three screenshots. The desktop
    screenshot defines the wide-viewport layout; the mobile screenshot defines
    the narrow-viewport layout; the tablet screenshot defines the intermediate.

R6. Reproduce the footer in full. Footers on real pages contain multi-column
    link lists, copyright notices, sponsor attributions, site-map links, and
    legal text. Copy every column, every link label, and every line of small
    print exactly as visible. Do not replace the real footer with a generic
    placeholder or a single-line summary — that is a faithfulness failure.

TASK
----
Produce a single complete HTML file following all instructions below.
Work through them in order: structure first, then ARIA, then JS.

