PART B — ARIA ATTRIBUTE FIXES (apply unconditionally)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

B1. Remove redundant ARIA
    - Remove role="navigation" from <nav> (implicit)
    - Remove role="main" from <main> (implicit)
    - Remove role="banner" from <header> (implicit)
    - Remove role="contentinfo" from <footer> (implicit)
    - Rule: never add role= to an element that already has that implicit role

B2. Multiple navigation regions
    - If more than one <nav> exists, each must have a unique aria-label
    - Example: <nav aria-label="Main">, <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">

B3. Multiple landmarks of same type
    - If more than one <aside> or <section> exists, each needs aria-label
    - If more than one <header> or <footer> inside sections, add aria-label

B4. Focus management baseline
    - Remove any tabindex values greater than 0 from all elements
    - tabindex="0" is acceptable on custom interactive elements
    - tabindex="-1" is acceptable for programmatic focus targets
    - tabindex="1" or higher: remove entirely

